## What a `type: ai-actor` instance is

**An AI actor memorial describes a specific versioned AI model** — typically a single release of a model from a single provider (a particular Claude version, a particular codex version + model, or a future external AI agent).

Versioning is intentionally **per-release**, not per-conversation-session.  An AI actor instance is the model version; the model is queryable as a graph citizen with version, capabilities, and provider organization.

Within a single AI actor instance, multiple **conversation sessions** occur but those are NOT separate actor memorials — the actor IS the model version, not the per-session execution.

AI Actor is a subtype of [`actor`](actor.md) → [`meta`](meta.md).

